        "original_id": "1d55f5a9-6e0f-5dbb-b805-62b309f9ee44",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Arthur Saint-Léon, Fanny Cerrito, Cesare Pugni, Diana Vishneva\n- Organizations: Mariinsky Ballet, Mariinsky Theatre, Vaganova Ballet Academy, St. Petersburg Imperial Ballet\n- Places: Paris, Saint Petersburg, Russia\n- Roles: Maître de Ballet, principal dancer\n- Works: Coppélia, La Vivandière, Markitenka\n\nFacts:\n- Arthur Saint-Léon was born on 17 September 1821 in Paris and died on 2 September 1870.\n- The Mariinsky Ballet was founded in the 18th century and was originally known as the Imperial Russian Ballet.\n- Arthur Saint-Léon served as Maître de Ballet of the St. Petersburg Imperial Ballet from 1859 to 1869.\n- Arthur Saint-Léon is famous for creating the choreography of the ballet Coppélia.\n- La Vivandière, known in Russia as Markitenka, is a one-act ballet with choreography by Arthur Saint-Léon and Fanny Cerrito and music by Cesare Pugni.\n- Diana Vishneva was born on 13 July 1976 and is a Russian ballet dancer.\n- The Mariinsky Ballet is the resident classical ballet company of the Mariinsky Theatre in Saint Petersburg, Russia.\n- The Mariinsky Ballet is one of the world's leading ballet companies.\n- The Mariinsky Ballet is the parent company of the Vaganova Ballet Academy, a leading international ballet school.\n- Diana Vishneva performs as a principal dancer with the Mariinsky Ballet, formerly known as the Kirov Ballet.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
